#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:1
msgid "Reviewing your numbers and producing the upload file"
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:3
msgid ""
"This page covers the two outputs the tool produces once a calculation is "
"complete - a spreadsheet for you to review, and the exact file the AEAT "
"portal accepts - and why they are separate things."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:7
msgid "Why there are two outputs, not one"
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:9
msgid ""
"The first output is for you. Before you commit to any numbers, you want "
"to see how each total was reached and adjust a figure if something looks "
"off. Your calculation is laid out in Google Sheets with a live formula "
"behind every total, so a corrected input recomputes everything that "
"depends on it in front of you, and your reviewed edits pull back into the"
" tool against the exact calculation the sheet was built from. The offline"
" `.xlsx` the tool can also produce is a fixed keepsake of the calculation"
" and its evidence, not a review surface. The walkthrough is [Review "
"calculations with Google Sheets](../how-to/review-with-google-sheets.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:19
msgid ""
"The second output is for the machine on the other end. AEAT accepts "
"uploads only in one precise text format, with every value at a fixed "
"position, rejected if it differs by a character. The tool builds that "
"file from your reviewed calculation on your own computer - generating the"
" file and submitting it are separate acts, and the tool never submits for"
" you. When it writes the file it reports a fingerprint of the exact "
"contents, so you can later prove which file you uploaded. The steps are "
"in [Upload your exported modelo at the AEAT portal](../how-to/file-at-"
"aeat.md)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:28
msgid ""
"One is a review surface; the other is a delivery format. Keeping them "
"apart is what lets each be good at what it does."
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:31
msgid "Where this sits in your filing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../explanation/reviewing-and-exporting.md:33
msgid ""
"These outputs come after the completeness check described in [Editing and"
" verifying a calculation](editing-and-verifying.md) - review and export "
"are worth doing only once the modelo is complete. Producing the upload "
"file is not the same as filing it; what happens after you have the file "
"is covered in [Recording a filing, and why the tool never files for "
"you](recording-a-filing-and-the-boundary.md)."
msgstr ""

